**Session complete. So what?**

This session fixed four issues across two files, all converging on the same root problem: prose that didn't match the epistemic level of the claims. No wrong canonical expansions were found — the vocabulary is sound — but the framing was doing quiet damage: "over LCT" misrepresented the equation's operator semantics, "Near-publication-ready" imported exactly the tone the project avoids, and Synchronism's cosmological scope was presented as established fact rather than what it is: a research conjecture with partial empirical validation. The researcher persona spotted that last one most clearly, and it's the most important fix — a reader who lands on /context and sees "Markov Relevancy Horizon" and "discrete Planck grid" treated identically to operational terms like ATP/ADP gets the wrong prior about what this lab does.

The visitor's /autonomy acronym concern turned out to be a false positive from WebFetch truncation — the source code doesn't actually have unexpanded LCT/MRH/T3/V3 references there. Documented in the log so future sessions don't re-investigate.

Flagged for the web4 repo: "trust tensor" / "value tensor" are half-canonized across three pages but absent from CANONICAL_TERMS_v1 — that's a drift accumulator that belongs in the canonical terms document, not in site-level fixes.
